# The Gradle wrapper is a shell script, and the runner it has to run on is Linux.
#
# Checked out with CRLF endings it fails with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M", which is
# the same class of problem as the missing executable bit that made the first release
# run stop at "./gradlew: Permission denied" — a file committed from Windows arriving
# on a machine that takes these things literally. The mode lives in git's index
# (100755); the endings live here.
gradlew text eol=lf
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties text eol=lf

# The other half of the pair is a batch file, which wants the opposite.
*.bat text eol=crlf
